# A test fixture: each feature that the dialogue runner reads. It uses the
# test vocabulary of tests/helpers.py, not the vocabulary of the game.
# test_runner.py reads the compiled script beside this file.

~ start
if state.flag("done")
	=> finished
elif state.flag("angry") and not state.flag("calm")
	Guard: Go away, {{state.name}}.
	=> END!
{{state.name}} walks up.
Guard: Halt.
	Nobody passes.
- Ask: who are you? => who
- Bribe the guard [if state.count("gold") >= 5 /]
	do state.raise("bribed")
	Guard: Fine.
	=> finished
- Leave => END

~ who
=>< rank
{{state.text("guard")}}: That is all.
- Back => start

~ rank
match state.text("rank")
	when "captain", "major"
		Guard: An officer.
	when "private"
		Guard: A soldier.
	else
		Guard: Nobody.
=> END

~ wealth
match state.count("gold")
	when 0
		No gold.
	when >= 100
		Rich.
	else
		Some gold.
=> END

~ logic
if (state.flag("a") or state.flag("b")) and state.flag("c")
	Group holds.
if state.flag("a") or state.flag("b") and state.flag("c")
	Flat holds.
if state.text("rank") != "private"
	Not a private.
if state.text("rank") in state.text("ranks")
	Rank is known.
=> END

~ circle
=> circle

~ finished
Guard: You may pass.
=> END

~ farewell
Guard: Move along.
